# The Freudenthal-Tits magic square and the Barton-Sudbery dimension formula for the exceptional Lie algebras. Pairing the
# octonions with each of the four division algebras gives the exceptional series F4, E6, E7 and E8, of dimensions fifty-
# two, seventy-eight, one hundred thirty-three and two hundred forty-eight, each nested inside the next. The dimension is
# forced by one formula: the triality algebra of the first factor plus the triality algebra of the octonions, twenty-eight,
# plus three times the product of the two dimensions, with the triality dimensions zero, two, nine and twenty-eight for
# the reals, complexes, quaternions and octonions. This file MODELS the exceptional series and the inclusion that climbs
# it, and PROVES the ceiling: climbing three steps from F4 reaches E8, which is the top and contains all the others, so the
# series has exactly four members. The Barton-Sudbery dimensions and the Freudenthal grading chain that nests each algebra
# in the next are then recorded as exact machine-integer counts. The ceiling theorem is quantified over the actual four-
# element type and proved by induction.

# The exceptional Lie algebras, the octonionic row of the magic square.
form exceptional
  case f-four
  case e-six
  case e-seven
  case e-eight

# The inclusion climbing the series: F4 sits in E6 sits in E7 sits in E8, the top.
task next
  take g, like exceptional
  like exceptional
  fork case, read g
    case f-four
      send back
        make e-six
    case e-six
      send back
        make e-seven
    case e-seven
      send back
        make e-eight
    case e-eight
      send back
        make e-eight

# THE EXCEPTIONAL CEILING: climbing three steps from any member reaches E8, next (next (next g)) = e-eight, for every g.
# So the exceptional series is four algebras tall and stops at E8, the largest exceptional Lie algebra. Proved by
# induction over the four members.
rule climbing-three-steps-reaches-e-eight
  seat g, like exceptional
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call next
        call next
          call next
            read g
      make e-eight
  fold g

# E8 IS THE TOP: it is the fixed point of the inclusion, next e-eight = e-eight.
rule e-eight-is-the-top
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call next
        make e-eight
      make e-eight
  calm hold

# THE BARTON-SUDBERY DIMENSIONS as machine-integer counts, dimension = tri(A) + tri(O) + 3 * dim(A) * dim(O), with
# tri(O) = 28. F4 from the reals: tri 0 plus 28 plus 3 * 1 * 8 = 0 + 28 + 24 = 52.
hold f-four-dimension-is-fifty-two
  call is-equal
    code 52
    call add
      code 28
      call multiply
        code 3
        call multiply
          code 1
          code 8

# E8 from the octonions: tri(O) 28 plus 28 plus 3 * 8 * 8 = 28 + 28 + 192 = 248.
hold e-eight-dimension-is-two-hundred-forty-eight
  call is-equal
    code 248
    call add
      code 28
      call add
        code 28
        call multiply
          code 3
          call multiply
            code 8
            code 8

# THE FREUDENTHAL GRADING that nests each algebra in the next. E6 is F4 plus the twenty-six of the exceptional Jordan
# algebra: 78 = 52 + 26.
hold e-six-is-f-four-plus-twenty-six
  call is-equal
    code 78
    call add
      code 52
      code 26

# E8 over E7 is the su(2) triple plus the fifty-six doublet: 248 = 133 + 3 + 112, with 112 the fifty-six times two.
hold e-eight-is-e-seven-plus-su-two-plus-the-doublet
  call is-equal
    code 248
    call add
      code 133
      call add
        code 3
        call multiply
          code 56
          code 2
